## spdx-correct.js

The *approach* behind `src/trustedlicenses/detection.py`'s `_correct_license_statement`
(reformat punctuation/whitespace/a version number already present in a free-text
license statement, then trust the result only once it validates as a real SPDX id) is
adapted from the validated-transform tier of spdx-correct.js
(https://github.com/jslicense/spdx-correct.js) -- no code from that project is
included verbatim; this project's transform/transposition tables were written fresh
in Python, and deliberately omit that library's separate "last resort"
substring-guessing tier.

